1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,570
So the dots that were
on that windshield

2
00:00:02,570 --> 00:00:04,038
are formed by air coolant.

3
00:00:04,038 --> 00:00:05,606
That's how tempered
glass is made.

4
00:00:05,606 --> 00:00:08,542
It goes through what's called
a [? lear ?] or a rolling

5
00:00:08,542 --> 00:00:11,312
conveyor, and it's heated
up very, very quickly,

6
00:00:11,312 --> 00:00:13,080
and then it's
cooled very quickly.

7
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:16,717
And it's cooled by this
array of compressed air jets

8
00:00:16,717 --> 00:00:20,154
on both sides that take it
from almost the transition

9
00:00:20,154 --> 00:00:21,455
temperature--

10
00:00:21,455 --> 00:00:23,657
it just about wants
to move but doesn't

11
00:00:23,657 --> 00:00:28,662
quite, down to room temperature
in three minutes or so.

12
00:00:28,662 --> 00:00:33,267
And that super-rapid cooling
is what generates that stress

13
00:00:33,267 --> 00:00:34,034
on the--

14
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:35,669
the difference
between the inside

15
00:00:35,669 --> 00:00:38,072
and the outside
temperature in the glass.

16
00:00:38,072 --> 00:00:40,107
And so it's air cooled,
but Prince Rupert

17
00:00:40,107 --> 00:00:44,245
drop is cooled by--
anyone want to guess?

18
00:00:44,245 --> 00:00:45,079
Water.

19
00:00:45,079 --> 00:00:46,714
Yeah, by water.

20
00:00:46,714 --> 00:00:49,683
So water is a better
coolant, right?

21
00:00:49,683 --> 00:00:53,354
So as a result, you
get a lot more stress

22
00:00:53,354 --> 00:00:56,223
embodied with the glass,
a lot more stress.

23
00:00:56,223 --> 00:00:58,659
And so that's
relevant because you

24
00:00:58,659 --> 00:01:01,896
don't want to make a window that
breaks with that kind of energy

25
00:01:01,896 --> 00:01:05,299
and so you get explosive
energy all over the place.

26
00:01:05,299 --> 00:01:08,035
So tempered glass is
engineered to fail.

27
00:01:08,035 --> 00:01:11,105
It's very strong,
but it's engineered

28
00:01:11,105 --> 00:01:13,941
to fail so that when it breaks,
it breaks into small pieces

29
00:01:13,941 --> 00:01:18,045
so that if you're walking along
the sidewalk and a skyscraper

30
00:01:18,045 --> 00:01:21,415
blows out a window, you don't
get huge shards of glass

31
00:01:21,415 --> 00:01:23,784
falling down and hurting people.

32
00:01:23,784 --> 00:01:26,086
You get little pellets
gently raining down,

33
00:01:26,086 --> 00:01:28,022
which isn't such a bad thing.

34
00:01:28,022 --> 00:01:29,456
[LAUGHTER]
